From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Afonchenko <undermove1@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 23:17:42 +0400
Subject: [PATCH 209/209] Meridian: Claude Code sessions outlive a crash of the
 browser

- A terminal host (the browser's binary, --meridian-term-host) keeps a second
  fd of every Workbench terminal's pty: a crash no longer closes the pty, so
  the programs in it (Claude Code mid-work) go on. While no browser reads them
  the host keeps their output; the reopened Workbench takes them back and
  shows them, instead of resuming the sessions anew. A clean quit still
  closes them (the profile's exit_type), unclaimed ones are hung up after 2 h.
- Mission Control's socket keeps its path per profile, and an adopted session
  keeps its token: its hooks reach the new browser (status, session id).
- The MCP bridge waits up to 45 s for a browser that went down instead of
  failing every call at once.
- macOS and Linux; Windows terminals are pseudoconsoles in the browser.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SwxrQ2eLfJ2bv8cCoG2va1
